{"role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "The Cloudwatch logs for the Lambda function do not contain any recent error messages, suggesting that the application is failing silently or the logs are not being properly captured.

Based on the evidence gathered, the root cause of the task-app application failure appears to be an incorrect configuration of the TABLE_NAME environment variable in the Lambda function. The function is attempting to access a DynamoDB table named "appdata-wrong" instead of the actual table named "appdata".

To resolve this issue, the TABLE_NAME environment variable should be updated to the correct table name. However, I will not perform this remediation action, as it requires explicit human approval."}]}
